/-!
# Residues above infinity: a Möbius transformation

On `y² = f(x) = x (x − 7)(x − 14)(x + 18)` (degree `4`, two places `∞±` above infinity),
`∫ x dx / y` has residues `∓1` at `∞±` only. Its residue divisor `∞₋ − ∞₊` is not torsion. The
substitution `t = 1/(x − 12)`, `w = y t²` (`mobCheck`, with `f(12) = −3600 = (60 i)²`) moves `∞±`
to the points `(0, ±1)` of `w² = G(t) = (1 + 12t)(1 + 5t)(1 − 2t)(1 + 30t)`. There
`decideLogT` (primes `13` and `73`) answers `some false`, and `decideLogT_mob_spec` transfers the
answer back: `∫ x dx / √(x (x − 7)(x − 14)(x + 18))` is **not elementary**.
-/

